# Act I

= A young person fights to escape an oppressive system — unaware that the rebellion itself is the inherited memory of the last scientists who built the world that imprisoned them.

## Sequence A

EXT. THE INSTITUTE - DAY

A vast decaying building. Nature reclaims the walls. [[This is a writer's note about the scene]]

INT. CENTRAL ROOM - DAY

KAEL (15, intense) stares at a wall of pale light.

KAEL
Something's wrong. Everything arrives too perfectly.

MIRA (15, warm) enters behind them.

MIRA
You're feeling it too?

KAEL
(chosen)
I was meant to find this.

~Singing in the darkness~
~A lullaby for the lost~

### Scene Group 1

EXT. THE GARDEN - NIGHT

Kael walks through simulated moonlight. The grass feels real. [[Another note about the garden]]

INT. THE CORE - DAY (400 YEARS EARLIER)

DR. ELENA VOSS (42, exhausted) works at a terminal. MARCUS CHEN (38, empathetic) enters.

MARCUS
They're at the gates. They want in.

ELENA
The project is too fragile. We can't compromise.

MARCUS
They're dying, Elena. We all are.

ELENA
(almost to herself)
The truth would kill them.

EXT. THE INSTITUTE - NIGHT (400 YEARS EARLIER)

Outsiders gather. Desperate. Hopeful.

INT. CENTRAL ROOM - NIGHT

Kael stands before the door. The Administrator's voice echoes.

ADMINISTRATOR (V.O.)
You don't understand what you'd be entering.

KAEL
I understand I was chosen.

The door opens.

                CUT TO:

.OPENING TITLES

> THE END <

===

# Act II

= The children discover the truth about their world.

